Z||000000||FAXKID||10-08-1999||09:43 PM||||  Does anyone know where a non-mechanic like myself,might find an engine diagrahm?I just had my 1986 gt rebuilt.When I drive it I hear a clicking sound.I looked under it and it looks like an engine cover missing.Inside it looks like cogs or gears.My problem is I don't know what to call the cover to order it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick||10-08-1999||10:07 PM||||<BR>Your best bet is to get a manual specific to the Fiero. Although it is not perfect, I recommend that you buy the <B>Haynes</B> publication entitled, <B>Pontiac Fiero</B>. It covers all models, '84-'88, and it really is quite informative. Here in Canada they can be found on occasion for $10, so you can probably find them for less in the States.<P>If you require something more intensive, you can always spend a few hours at your local library.  ||||reg||3
Z||000002||fiero56||10-08-1999||10:46 PM||||I was at the "local library" a few days ago working on some papers, when I noticed just down the aisle from me were these big huge blue books.  I'm talking dictionary size, Webster's biggest, they bend when you pick them up, and they're hardback.  Looked up the fiero, and they showed how to do just about everything.  Closest to a factory manual I have found yet. I'm gonna' check one out in the coming weeks when I replace my clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RZURCTN||10-08-1999||11:13 PM||||Haynes manuals cost about $16 around here.  I am really not too happy with them either.  Every time I need to know the real juicy stuff it says, "Consult your local dealer or Parts service."  *^$%* that!! The dealer will charge me $65 an hour just to tell me they can't fix it and the new part will cost $300 and they can have there in 4 to 6 weeks, unless I care to pay for Express Delivery, in which case they can have it in 3 weeks!  I hate car dealers!!!  I hate Haynes for directing me to a car dealer!!!  Sorry guys, I had to get that off my chest.  Maybe I'll go to the library!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||10-08-1999||11:48 PM||||Why doesnt anybody buy the factory manual. They are still available. I admit they are a little pricey but well worth it. I buy them for all my cars.||||reg||1
